{
    "background_story": "Murphy had always been a bit of a struggling artist, working multiple part-time jobs to make ends meet while he pursued his passion for painting. Despite his best efforts, he found himself falling behind on his rent and utility bills. Before he knew it, he was in arrears, owing his landlord and the electric company a substantial amount of money. Feeling overwhelmed and anxious, Murphy considered giving up on his dreams. However, with the help of a local non-profit organization, he was able to get back on his feet. They provided him with financial assistance and guidance, helping him to create a budget and get his debt under control. With renewed determination, Murphy continued to paint, eventually landing a few commissioned pieces that helped him pay off his debts. He learned a valuable lesson about the importance of financial responsibility, but also about the power of perseverance and community support.",
